

                        T H I S S A L A
                        ---------------


        The game of THISSALA is a fantasy game similar to ADVENTURE and
ZORK.  The game was written to run under AOS or AOS/VS by David
Auerbach, Paul Chiasson, and Peter Macaulay of Data General's Corporate
Systems Engineering Group.

        The fundamental difference between THISSALA and other games 
is that the goal in THISSALA is not just to get all the treasure, but to
accomplish a substantial feat, that is, to save the world from the forces
of evil, and restore the power of good.  Hidden somewhere in the land
is a parchment describing the tale of THAMOS and MAKASSAR.  This scroll
holds the initial clues to what must be done.

        In addition to the above difference, THISSALA has an enhanced
parser compared to ADVENTURE and the DG version of ZORK. The game is also
substantially larger, consisting of close to 1000 rooms and 400 objects. 
In addition, the player now has attributes. These are:

        POWER           how strong the player is.  If POWER goes to zero,
                        the player dies.  POWER is gained by eating.
                        POWER is lost by dieing and by being wounded by
                        an evil creature.  The amount of damage that
                        the player can inflict upon an evil creature is
                        also determined in part by the player's POWER
                        level

        COOR            the player's coordination.  Coordination is
                        gained by playing (the longer you play, the
                        greater your coordination) and by doing feats
                        that normally demonstrate some coordination.
                        COOR will be decreased by drinking.  How often
                        you hit an evil creature, and vice versa, is
                        determined by the player's coordination value

        MAGIC           the player's magic ability.  MAGIC is increased
                        by reading specific books, and by learning magic
                        spells.  Magic can be used in various parts of
                        the maze to solve problems and accomplish feats

        WISDOM          who the hell knows?

        KNOWLEDGE       is a measure of how much of the game the player
                        has explored.  Knowledge is the percent of
                        rooms visited by the player during the current
                        session
